  "mathematical_coherence_checks": {
    "stationary_uniqueness": "Existing HessianStrongConvexity produces StrongConvexOn univ kappa^-1 V from actual C2 lower Hessian. StrongConvexFirstOrder.gradient_inner_lower_bound supplies <grad V(z)-grad V(p),z-p> >= kappa^-1 norm(z-p)^2. Difference of the two stationarity equations gives norm(z-p)^2+eta*<gradient difference,z-p>=0. Since 1+eta*kappa^-1>0 (kappa>=1,eta>0), z=p. No Nontrivial/dimension-positive premise or new generic unique wrapper is required.",
    "same_witness": "A single actual current32 invocation can supply one p and the literal rho/R/r/Z/q tuple. Adding uniquely stationary output permits later opaque stationary witness identification by a proved equality, rather than silently identifying existential choices. No proof body has yet established that invocation here.",
    "explicit_log_domain": "Current32 actual q log q L1 gamma implies exp(-rho) log q=Z(q log q) L1 gamma. Positive Z gives exp(-rho) L1 independently from rho>=0 domination or integral_undef contradiction. integrable_tilted_iff yields log q L1 under actual r. log q=-rho-log Z plus actual r probability gives rho L1 internally.",
    "canonical_KL": "TiltedKL with base gamma, f=-rho,g=0 needs actual left measurability, exp-left L1, exp-zero L1, and explicit normalized logratio L1 under left actual tilt. All follow internally. Gamma is SigmaFinite/NeZero from probability. Right zero tilt=gamma. Existing producer gives genuine KL !=top with toReal integral; TiltedLogRatio gives AE llr identity, hence canonical llr L1. No weaker toReal-only RNLogRatio theorem is used as finiteness evidence.",
    "entropy_formulas": "Actual tilt integral writes integral_r log q=integral_gamma q log q. Since rho and log q L1 under actual probability r, pointwise log q=-rho-log Z yields -integral_r rho-log Z. Probability masses cancel canonical finite-measure correction and no affine normalizer remains.",
    "zero_and_large_eta": "E0 has the unique vector, rho=0,Z=1,q=1,r=gamma, KL=0 and all canonical logratio integrability conclusions. Every positive eta finite real, with no numerical cap; stationary uniqueness coefficient stays positive. No positive residual Lipschitz L is introduced."
  },
